{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1257 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "54c239e244ea4b51d96d8d27bfcac929952c6a4b0b595e4b8affccbe381d9630" :edb/db-before-t 1256 :edb/db-after-t 1257 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534569 50 #inst "2026-10-12T03:20:19.161Z" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186140358 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425994 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186140358 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425994 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186140577 1078 #edb/ref 17592186140579 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142510 1071 "Find the value of $5\\times \\dfrac{1}{12}$." 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186142510 1071 "Find the value of $5\\times \\dfrac{1}{12}.$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142511 1071 "Multiply $\\dfrac{2}{3}\\times 3$." 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186142511 1071 "Multiply $\\dfrac{2}{3}\\times 3.$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142511 1074 "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2\\times 3}{3} = \\dfrac{6}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify this fraction by interpreting\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 6 3\n$$\n\nas a division:\n\n$$\n6\\div 3 =2\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186142511 1074 "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2\\times 3}{3} = \\dfrac{6}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify this fraction by interpreting $\\dfrac 6 3$ as a division:\n\n$$\n6\\div 3 =2\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142512 1071 "Multiply $\\dfrac{1}{6}\\times 4$." 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186142512 1071 "Multiply $\\dfrac{1}{6}\\times 4.$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142512 1074 "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1\\times 4}{6} = \\dfrac{4}{6}\n$$\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we can divide the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4\\div 2}{6\\div 2} = \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186142512 1074 "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1\\times 4}{6} = \\dfrac{4}{6}\n$$\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we can divide the numerator and denominator by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4\\div 2}{6\\div 2} = \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142772 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426009 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142772 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426010 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142773 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426006 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142773 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426007 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142774 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426011 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142775 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426008 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186142997 1050 420.0 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186143196 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186143196 1071 "Expressed as a mixed number in its lowest terms, $6 \\cdot \\frac{7}{8} =$ {{field-1}}." 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186143196 1071 "Expressed as a mixed number in its lowest terms, $6\\times \\frac{7}{8}=${{field-1}}." 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186143196 1074 "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 7}{8}=\\frac{42}{8}\n$$\n\nWe then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{42}{8}=\\frac{42÷2}{8÷2}=\\frac{21}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{21}{4}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n21÷4=5\\,\\text{R}\\,1=5\\,\\frac{1}{4}\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186143268 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186143268 1071 "$3\\times \\frac{1}{6}=$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186143268 1071 "What is $3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{6}$?" 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186143268 1074 "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 1}{6}=\\frac{3}{6}\n$$\n\nWe then reduce this fraction to its lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{6}=\\frac{3÷3}{6÷3}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186144029 1064 "We can use models to multiply fractions by whole numbers. But can we do this without using models?\n\nAs it turns out, models give us vital clues on how this should be done!\n\nTo demonstrate, let's take a look at the fraction model for\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 2 9 \\times 3\n$$\n\n![](images/47/4700c7ddbdc849a73d69ba41d2d716218f1fb181e8e5e9b8757392db6d9a6243.png)\n\nIn the answer, we end up with\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{2}}\\times {\\color{red}{3}} = 6\n$$\n\nparts, and the denominator remains the same. This is always the case.\n\nTherefore, to multiply a fraction by a whole number, we follow the following steps:\n\n> **Step 1**: We multiply the numerator by the whole number.\n> **Step 2**: We keep the denominator the same.\n\nUsing these steps, we can figure out the answer without using models:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}2}{9}{\\color{red}\\,\\times 3\\,} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}{2}}{\\color{red}\\,\\times 3\\,}}{9} = \\dfrac{6}{9}\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 false] [17592186144029 1064 "We can use models to multiply fractions by whole numbers. But can we do this without using models?\n\nAs it turns out, models give us vital clues on how this should be done!\n\nTo demonstrate, let's take a look at the fraction model for $\\dfrac 2 9 \\times 3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/47/4700c7ddbdc849a73d69ba41d2d716218f1fb181e8e5e9b8757392db6d9a6243.png)\n\nIn the answer, we end up with ${\\color{blue}{2}}\\times {\\color{red}{3}} = 6$ parts, and the denominator remains the same. This is always the case. \n\nTherefore, to multiply a fraction by a whole number, we follow the following steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We multiply the numerator by the whole number.\n\n**Step 2**: We keep the denominator the same.\n\nUsing these steps, we can figure out the answer without using models:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}2}{9}{\\color{red}\\,\\times 3\\,} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}{2}}{\\color{red}\\,\\times 3\\,}}{9} =  \\dfrac{6}{9}\n$$" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425981 1080 "\\frac{5}{8}" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425981 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425981 1083 #uuid "04d85cf7-d690-5c73-a893-ab44d3179b9a" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425982 1080 "\\frac{18}{11}" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425982 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425982 1083 #uuid "09f3754e-b1c1-5f1e-ace2-3c70c5d86e12" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425983 1080 "\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425983 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425983 1083 #uuid "1a1bd069-87c9-5de3-8c9a-8c74d32862a1" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425984 1080 "3" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425984 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425984 1083 #uuid "2096b976-0bc9-5b59-9173-c7565523a588" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425985 1080 "2" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425985 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425985 1083 #uuid "20e59d40-16bd-52d3-b1d5-61eff3c0c81d" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425986 1080 "6" 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425986 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534569 17592186045417 true] [17592186425986 1083 #uuid "2b524dea-2f19-5de3-b09c-7f9fd